EXP01_minute_only
EXP01_minute_only is a LightGBM classifier experiment that focuses on minute derived curve features. It uses IEM minute series only. The purpose is establish a curve only baseline. On the test split it achieved accuracy 0.732, balanced accuracy 0.700, YES precision 0.665, and YES recall 0.572. On validation it achieved accuracy 0.741 and balanced accuracy 0.703. This result shows moderate skill with useful signal. It serves as a baseline comparator for later variants. These notes emphasize leak-safe comparison across batches and clarify precision/recall tradeoffs for future revisions and ablations.
Clarified interpretation: The input features and model family are exactly as stated above; no additional signals are introduced. The model makes a single binary decision at the cutoff: has the daily maximum (Tmax) already occurred? YES precision reflects avoiding false early-peak calls, while YES recall reflects avoiding missed late-heating cases. Use these metrics strictly for relative ranking within the same split and thresholds, not as a trading PnL claim. If this variant underperforms, it usually means the added hypothesis is noisy, weak, or needs better calibration. Compare it to the closest baseline in this batch and focus on balanced accuracy and the precision/recall tradeoff together.

